<zk>
	<zscript><![CDATA[
		void echoRange(org.zkoss.zkmax.zul.Daterangebox b) {
			if (b.getBeginValue() == null || b.getEndValue() == null) {
				echo.setValue("incomplete");
			} else {
				java.text.SimpleDateFormat f = new java.text.SimpleDateFormat("yyyy/MM/dd");
				echo.setValue(f.format(b.getBeginValue()) + "~" + f.format(b.getEndValue()));
			}
		}
	]]></zscript>
	<label multiline="true">
		Steps to reproduce:
		1. Click the readonly datebox — its calendar opens and a date can be picked.
		2. Click the readonly daterangebox's calendar button, then pick two days.

		- Expected: both behave the same. readonly means "you can't type", not "you can't
			pick": the popup opens and the pick commits, as with Combobox / Bandbox / Datebox
			/ Timepicker.
		- Bug: the daterangebox is the only one of the family that closes off its popup when
			readonly, so no range can be picked at all.

		The buttons sit above the boxes so an open popup can never cover them. The timer
			reports the server's isOpen() without a pointer event — any click outside the
			popup closes it first, which would make the reading meaningless.
		Guards: setOpen(true) must open a readonly box, and disabled must still block the
			popup outright — and a click on a disabled box must not even reach the server
			(the label below stays empty; the editable box fills it).
	</label>
	<hlayout>
		<button id="btnOpen" label="setOpen(true) on readonly + report isOpen"
			onClick='drbRo.setOpen(true); tmOpen.start()'/>
		<label id="echoOpen"/>
	</hlayout>
	<timer id="tmOpen" running="false" delay="600" repeats="false"
		onTimer='echoOpen.setValue(String.valueOf(drbRo.isOpen()))'/>
	<datebox id="dbRo" readonly="true"/>
	<daterangebox id="drbRo" readonly="true" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		onChange='echoRange(self)'/>
	<!-- the onClick listeners are what make the client send onClick at all: the
		event is registered with no CE_IMPORTANT flag, so with no server listener
		nothing leaves the browser and a disabled box's wasted round-trip would be
		invisible -->
	<daterangebox id="drbEdit" format="yyyy/MM/dd" onClick='echoClick.setValue(self.getId())'/>
	<daterangebox id="drbDisabled" disabled="true" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		onClick='echoClick.setValue(self.getId())'/>
	<label id="echo"/>
	<label id="echoClick"/>
</zk>
